            r2_bias_s_clientes: `Your sample already rides: it may be less price-sensitive and value the removable battery less.`,
            r2_bias_s_pequena: `With 300 people, the intervals are wide.`,
            r2_bias_s_redes: `Your sample is brand followers: they may prefer Urdin more than the average shopper.`,
            r2_brief: `The study is in the lab below: part-worths by segment with their 95% intervals, willingness to pay, importances and a share simulator running on your estimates. Configure the Hiri from components, set the price and decide how many to build for April–August (8,000 at most). Whatever is left in August is sold in the autumn at €180 off, and anything still unsold in 2028 is cleared at a €500 loss per bicycle; whatever is missing, Tornell will sell.`,
            r2_debate: `Do you design for the 65% who commute (price-sensitive, value weight and perhaps a removable battery) or for the 35% of enthusiasts (who pay for range and the central motor)? If two designs fall within the study’s intervals, which risk would you rather run? And remember: willingness to pay is not price; the best price depends on Tornell and on your costs.`,
            r2_econ_title: `Components, costs and net price`,
            r2_known_1: `Costs, weights and what Urdin keeps per bicycle (tables below). The Tornell stays at €2,290.`,
            r2_known_2: `Seasonality: April–August holds 5.9 of the year’s 12 months of sales; September–December, 3.8.`,
            r2_live: `Your Hiri: %KG% kg, costs %UC%, keeps %NET% net and %MG% of margin per bicycle. The study’s raw forecast for April–August: %F% bicycles; chosen run: %Q%.`,
